## Why This Is Asked

Observability is critical for CNPA; end-to-end tracing helps identify latency sources across HTTP, DB, and Kafka.

## Key Concepts

- Distributed tracing
- OpenTelemetry SDKs and exporters
- Trace context propagation headers and Kafka headers
- Sampling strategies
- End-to-end verification under load

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js OpenTelemetry setup sketch
const tracer = opentelemetry.trace.getTracer('cnpa');
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http', { attributes: { 'http.method': req.method }});
  res.on('finish', () => span.end());
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ensure producer retries don’t split traces?
- How would you visualize traces and correlate with latency metrics?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design safe, minimal, observable feature flag gating in CNPA stacks under concurrency.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and per-request gating
- Centralized flag store vs per-instance cache
- TTL-based cache and cache invalidation
- Canary rollout and rollback criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple gate helper
const FLAG_KEY = 'beta_feature_enabled';
async function isBetaEnabled(redis, cache, ttl = 1000) {
  let v = cache.get(FLAG_KEY);
  if (typeof v !== 'boolean') {
    v = await redis.get(FLAG_KEY);
    cache.set(FLAG_KEY, v, ttl);
  }
  return Boolean(v);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you migrate flags without downtime?
- How would you verify correctness under bursty load?

